<cell id="cell-0"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type># M5 L5: Document Ingestion and Parsing

**Build an idempotent ingestion service with content-hash dedupe and a DLQ.**

Duration: 90 min.  No API keys.</cell id="cell-0>
<cell id="cell-1"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## Plain English (the 12-year-old version)

**Ingestion** is the front door of every search system. Documents come in as text files, web pages, Word docs — and you need to clean them up, store them somewhere, and never accidentally store the same document twice.

The two non-negotiable rules: **(1) running the pipeline twice gives the same result** (idempotency), and **(2) one bad document never stops the whole batch** (dead-letter queue). Get those two right and most production failures disappear.</cell id="cell-1>
<cell id="cell-2"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## The 5 things to know

1. **Parse, normalize, dedupe, persist** — the four sub-problems, in that order.
2. **Content-hash dedupe** — SHA-256 of the normalized text; same hash = same doc.
3. **Idempotency** — re-running is safe; same input = same store state.
4. **Dead-letter queue** — bad docs go to a side channel, never silently dropped.
5. **Version your parsers** — silent parse changes corrupt the index; log every parse.</cell id="cell-2>
<cell id="cell-3"># === Standard setup ===
import sys, importlib.util
from pathlib import Path

def find_root(p):
    while p != p.parent:
        if (p / 'lessons').exists() and (p / 'SYLLABUS.md').exists():
            return p
        p = p.parent
    return Path.cwd()

ROOT = find_root(Path.cwd())
sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))

_p = ROOT / 'lessons' / 'm05-ingestion' / 'L5-document-ingestion.py'
_spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('L5', _p)
_L5 = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)
sys.modules['L5'] = _L5
_spec.loader.exec_module(_L5)

print(f'Setup OK. Lesson module: {_L5.LESSON_NUMBER}')</cell id="cell-3>
